-- Priest Shadow rework (docs/reworks/priest-shadow-rework.md sec 4.1,
-- .agents/plans/priest-rework/priest-rework.SHADOW.md "ID map"/"WP-0 prep") - hand-written
-- world-DB content for Tentacle of Madness (creature_template/creature_template_model aren't part
-- of apps/dbc-tools' generate.py pipeline, same treatment Divine Star's 300100 got in
-- rev_1789821533430365647.sql, which this row is cloned from).

-- Tentacle of Madness (300102, npc_pri_tentacle_of_madness in spell_priest_shadow.cpp), summoned
-- by spell 200245 (Tentacles of Madness talent, 3,0). Guardian, not a projectile trigger.
-- unit_flags = NOT_SELECTABLE | NON_ATTACKABLE (33554434), the DK Rune Weapon (27893) combination.
-- Both bits are only ever checked on the *target* side of Unit::_IsValidAttackTarget, so they give
-- the design doc's "Not targetable, not attackable" without touching what the tentacle may cast at.
-- Deliberately NOT Divine Star's IMMUNE_TO_PC | IMMUNE_TO_NPC (33555200): those two are checked on
-- the *caster* side too (Unit.cpp _IsValidAttackTarget "check flags" block), so they made the
-- tentacle unable to attack anything at all and its Mind Flay failed SPELL_FAILED_BAD_TARGETS on
-- every tick. Divine Star never hit this because it casts as the owner, not as itself.
-- "Generates no threat ... holds no threat table of its own" is unaffected (no threat is ever
-- generated by the tentacle's own casts; see npc_pri_tentacle_of_madness). flags_extra = CIVILIAN | NO_XP (66), deliberately NOT including
-- CREATURE_FLAG_EXTRA_TRIGGER (0x80) - see rev_1789821533430365647.sql's own note on this exact
-- bug (Unit::BuildValuesUpdateForPlayerWithFlag force-overrides UNIT_FIELD_DISPLAYID to the
-- invisible model for every non-GM observer when TRIGGER is set, bypassing creature_template_model
-- entirely; docs/bugs-and-fixes.md's `CREATURE_FLAG_EXTRA_TRIGGER` entry).
-- Display id 15788 (Eye Tentacle 15726's own model, PLAN sec 1 user call 2026-09-21) - its
-- creature_model_info row already exists (bounding_radius 0.96, combat_reach 2.5), verified
-- against data/sql/base/db_world/creature_model_info.sql, so no model_info insert here.
-- No DELETE here - creature_template is on this repo's SQL linter's do-not-delete list
-- (apps/codestyle/codestyle-sql.py's `not_delete`), and this is a first-time INSERT, not an edit to
-- an existing row, so there's no matching UPDATE...WHERE to fall back on either. An upsert is both
-- idempotent and never deletes.
